{title: 399 - Beneath the Forms of Outward Rite}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #399 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 399}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Beneath the [Bb/D]forms [Ab/C]of [Bb/D]outward [Eb]rite
[Bb/D]Thy [Eb]supper, [Bb]Lord, [Ab/C]is [Eb]spread
[Eb/G]In [Ab]every [Eb]quiet [Gm]upper room
[Cm]Where fainting souls are [Eb]fed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]The [Gm]bread [Eb]is [Bb/D]always consecrate
[Bb/D]Which [Eb]men [Cm]divide [Ab/C]with [Eb]men;
[Eb/G]And every act of [Gm]brotherhood
[Cm]Repeats [Fm/Ab]Thy [Cm]feast again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]The [Gm]blessed [Eb]cup is [Ab/C]only [Eb]passed
[Bb/D]True [Eb]memory [Ab/C]of [Eb]Thee,
[Eb/G]When [Ab]life [Bb7/F]anew [Eb]pours [Gm]out [Ab]its [Gm/Bb]wine
[Cm]With rich [Fm/Ab]sufficiency.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]O [Gm]Master, [Bb/D]through [Ab/C]these [Bb/D]symbols [Eb]shared,
[Bb/D]Thine [Eb]own [Cm]dear [Bb]self [Ab/C]impart,
[Eb/G]That [Ab]in [Bb7/F]our [Eb]daily [Gm]life [Ab]may [Gm/Bb]flame
[Cm]The passion of Thy [Eb]heart.
{end_of_verse}
